#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119577 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abef3da6-252e-51e4-b816-9ef7233b9a5d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Vector Form and a Plane in Dot Product Form"}] :question/id #uuid "1d809050-9477-5de6-8c95-7294804e7b69" :question/math-academy-id "e-4943" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equations\n\n$$\nl: \\mathbf{r} = \\langle 5,3,-4 \\rangle + t \\langle 4,-2,-3 \\rangle, \\qquad \t\\Pi: \\mathbf{r} \\cdot \\langle -7,5,1 \\rangle = -65.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 5+4t , 3-2t, -4-3t \\rangle.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 5+4t , 3-2t, -4-3t \\rangle$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-7,5,1⟩ & =-65 \\\\ ⟨5+4t,3-2t,-4-3t⟩\\cdot ⟨-7,5,1⟩ & =-65 \\\\ -7(5+4t)+5(3-2t)+(-4-3t) & =-65 \\\\ -35-28t+15-10t-4-3t & =-65 \\\\ -41t & =-41 \\\\ t & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the position vector $\\mathbf{p}$ of the intersection point is obtained by substituting $t=1$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨5+4(1),3-2(1),-4-3(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨9,1,-7⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(9 , 1, -7).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119578 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "caf29808-4551-56a0-ac86-a4587a06fc0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line and a Plane Given in Other Forms"}] :question/id #uuid "c1576b30-9142-5884-b654-7ade7a765ec7" :question/math-academy-id "e-4944" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equations\n\n$$\nl: \\mathbf{r} = \\langle 1,3,1 \\rangle + t \\langle 2,1,0 \\rangle, \\qquad  \\Pi:4x-3y+2z-7 = 0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 1+2t , 3+t, 1 \\rangle .\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-3y+2z-7 & =0 \\\\ 4x-3y+2z & =7 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨4,-3,2⟩ & =7 \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨4,-3,2⟩ & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 1+2t , 3+t, 1 \\rangle$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨4,-3,2⟩ & =7 \\\\ ⟨1+2t,3+t,1⟩\\cdot ⟨4,-3,2⟩ & =7 \\\\ 4(1+2t)-3(3+t)+2\\cdot 1 & =7 \\\\ 4+8t-9-3t+2 & =7 \\\\ 5t & =10 \\\\ t & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $\\mathbf{p}$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨1+2(2),3+(2),1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,5,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(5 , 5, 1).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119579 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e761b5-ec1c-549d-b726-e0909cfe460b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Parametric Form and a Plane in Cartesian Form"}] :question/id #uuid "f952e670-a673-5c15-913b-c396e8885142" :question/math-academy-id "e-4945" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equations\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083348/assets/2989739b62112c05f49beb975eb9039d1bbc7fca39ffd4d0adc058c7cf1cbb41.png)" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+4y+6z+25 & =0 \\\\ 3(3-4t)+4(-1+2t)+6(2+3t)+25 & =0 \\\\ 9-12t-4+8t+12+18t+25 & =0 \\\\ 14t & =-42 \\\\ t & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $\\mathbf{p}$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=-3$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=3-4(-3)=15 \\\\ y=-1+2(-3)=-7 \\\\ z=2+3(-3)=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $P(15,-7,-7).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387645 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abef3da6-252e-51e4-b816-9ef7233b9a5d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Vector Form and a Plane in Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02335c7f-58d3-594e-9025-e77d2b6b1f89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,5,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387647} {:answer/id #uuid "f9506b63-8fa9-5c67-b86c-a3f87456ee92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,5,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387648} {:answer/id #uuid "566d37e9-07ac-568b-b305-b71b19df247c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,7,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387649} {:answer/id #uuid "5fda1781-0421-56f4-a55a-476bf2136d75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387650} {:answer/id #uuid "d7fd3367-5165-591e-a1c4-d798c3288854" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,1,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387651}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "02335c7f-58d3-594e-9025-e77d2b6b1f89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,5,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387647} :answer-field/id #uuid "67b7fb82-dedf-5df6-810f-b039da558d9d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387646}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "310a805e-d3a4-5eae-9540-0ee13a3dc212" :question/math-academy-id "q-108309" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨2,3,-1⟩+t⟨-1,2,3⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨-2,1,4⟩=11.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨2-t,3+2t,-1+3t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨2-t,3+2t,-1+3t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-2,1,4⟩ & =11 \\\\ ⟨2-t,3+2t,-1+3t⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,1,4⟩ & =11 \\\\ -2(2-t)+1(3+2t)+4(-1+3t) & =11 \\\\ -4+2t+3+2t-4+12t & =11 \\\\ 16t & =16 \\\\ t & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=1$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨2-1,3+2(1),-1+3(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,5,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(1,5,2).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387652 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abef3da6-252e-51e4-b816-9ef7233b9a5d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Vector Form and a Plane in Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98729640-d11c-57fe-b316-27485116f69d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,-1,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387654} {:answer/id #uuid "ae8eb77c-6b88-5cfe-b984-034b6b32d4bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,3,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387655} {:answer/id #uuid "136cb6b5-7e4a-5eb7-98f5-004f40e9e211" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5,5,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387656} {:answer/id #uuid "aa2791b2-66c4-5ec5-8735-1e18b0d843b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387657} {:answer/id #uuid "2ccb4777-a636-5447-a5d9-f3ab9b925214" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-8,7,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387658}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ccb4777-a636-5447-a5d9-f3ab9b925214" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-8,7,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387658} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb2ddc0f-27fb-57ab-b8fc-48c5d3b48be2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387653}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8e5fe668-3628-59a7-b261-da619f1e8497" :question/math-academy-id "q-108310" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨-2,3,0⟩+t⟨3,-2,1⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨4,1,-3⟩=-19.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨-2+3t,3-2t,t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨-2+3t,3-2t,t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨4,1,-3⟩ & =-19 \\\\ ⟨-2+3t,3-2t,t⟩\\cdot ⟨4,1,-3⟩ & =-19 \\\\ 4(-2+3t)+1(3-2t)-3t & =-19 \\\\ -8+12t+3-2t-3t & =-19 \\\\ 7t & =-14 \\\\ t & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=-2$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨-2+3(-2),3-2(-2),(-2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-8,7,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(-8,7,-2).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338723 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abef3da6-252e-51e4-b816-9ef7233b9a5d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Vector Form and a Plane in Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ff1b670-d9ce-578f-abed-beb705375599" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,1,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338725} {:answer/id #uuid "c2f5a6ad-f90e-57b3-9d8a-f1d55a9c1f3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,-5,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338726} {:answer/id #uuid "8d6729de-aff7-5c4c-98ad-1bb06eb79a23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,-2,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338727} {:answer/id #uuid "eac8ebca-c530-5195-acb2-b6292ade13da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338728} {:answer/id #uuid "4f6b7658-2157-5f1b-b131-5b91d1e140f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,-8,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338729}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d6729de-aff7-5c4c-98ad-1bb06eb79a23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,-2,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338727} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f06fdb5-06f0-5457-8b29-4b3079bc722a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338724}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8d28c265-18d6-5656-afcf-7f8222829274" :question/math-academy-id "q-108311" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨5,-2,3⟩+t⟨0,3,-1⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨1,3,-2⟩=-7.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨5,-2+3t,3-t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨5,-2+3t,3-t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨1,3,-2⟩ & =-7 \\\\ ⟨5,-2+3t,3-t⟩\\cdot ⟨1,3,-2⟩ & =-7 \\\\ 5+3(-2+3t)+(-2)(3-t) & =-7 \\\\ 5-6+9t-6+2t & =-7 \\\\ 11t & =0 \\\\ t & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=0$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨5,-2+3(0),3-0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,-2,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(5,-2,3).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338730 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abef3da6-252e-51e4-b816-9ef7233b9a5d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Vector Form and a Plane in Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad1f5c5e-9bfc-542f-b83d-9cd12da5c2e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-7,4,-9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338732} {:answer/id #uuid "031f0ab7-98e5-5ef1-b694-26f424e0c1fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,0,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338733} {:answer/id #uuid "9a0767ba-c8fe-5d02-98cb-a2daad8cd428" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,2,-5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338734} {:answer/id #uuid "b90c5c3a-2f79-5901-856b-ccae222540c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(8,-2,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338735} {:answer/id #uuid "c6e8c10b-4c6c-548e-8a40-af66b3fc3888" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338736}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad1f5c5e-9bfc-542f-b83d-9cd12da5c2e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-7,4,-9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338732} :answer-field/id #uuid "5bd20147-884b-5aad-8617-b8c00cdeb58e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338731}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "aae7d446-6165-5274-a5d2-5622980a25ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-108313" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨3,0,-1⟩+t⟨5,-2,4⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨0,1,-2⟩=22.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨3+5t,-2t,-1+4t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨3+5t,-2t,-1+4t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨0,1,-2⟩ & =22 \\\\ ⟨3+5t,-2t,-1+4t⟩\\cdot ⟨0,1,-2⟩ & =22 \\\\ 0(3+5t)+1(-2t)+(-2)(-1+4t) & =22 \\\\ -2t+2-8t & =22 \\\\ -10t & =20 \\\\ t & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=-2$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨3+5(-2),-2(-2),-1+4(-2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-7,4,-9⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(-7,4,-9).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387659 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e761b5-ec1c-549d-b726-e0909cfe460b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Parametric Form and a Plane in Cartesian Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b6af5075-3f00-5b3e-b98d-3caab5a37adb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-4,-1,8)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387661} {:answer/id #uuid "6850bd1d-b068-5f7b-8fee-72a5ed76e4aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,-3,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387662} {:answer/id #uuid "9dc699a6-ddfd-5104-bda8-ad435c6ee34f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,-2,6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387663} {:answer/id #uuid "23d56610-6a2a-5a66-b792-2a883a6e0483" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,-4,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387664} {:answer/id #uuid "dd475f9c-5c3d-537a-a0c0-e7d3e2e12d11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387665}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b6af5075-3f00-5b3e-b98d-3caab5a37adb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-4,-1,8)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387661} :answer-field/id #uuid "dbdd719a-4878-57c6-bcfd-7fa1eae01e15" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387660}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5e78c76d-4b0c-5299-a8c9-57ef8fd9ba3e" :question/math-academy-id "q-108325" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:{\\begin{aligned}x=2-3t \\\\ y=-3+t \\\\ z=4+2t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:3x+y-4z+45=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+y-4z+45 & =0 \\\\ 3(2-3t)+(-3+t)-4(4+2t) & =-45 \\\\ 6-9t-3+t-16-8t & =-45 \\\\ -16t & =-32 \\\\ t & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=2$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=2-3(2)=-4 \\\\ y=-3+2=-1 \\\\ z=4+2(2)=8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is  $P(-4,-1,8).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338751 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e761b5-ec1c-549d-b726-e0909cfe460b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Parametric Form and a Plane in Cartesian Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0685c34e-7f8c-542c-a8df-082d2bd2d0dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-6,15,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338753} {:answer/id #uuid "0ebcf735-1d00-575e-9786-8bd7db6f13d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3,13,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338754} {:answer/id #uuid "9c7549da-aa05-5f9a-b970-554a5ae24af8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338755} {:answer/id #uuid "55bad4ad-1cc1-5384-974a-a376f90f80bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,9,-5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338756} {:answer/id #uuid "4847ee0f-9e5c-5369-bbda-8d74f3fffe1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(18,-1,-10)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338757}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0685c34e-7f8c-542c-a8df-082d2bd2d0dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-6,15,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338753} :answer-field/id #uuid "6aabbaa0-da27-5e13-92cc-3d64261bc76d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338752}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "36683b19-26fd-5526-a537-6298e5ac4183" :question/math-academy-id "q-108337" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:{\\begin{aligned}x=9-3t \\\\ y=5+2t \\\\ z=-7+t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:4x+3y+5z-11=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+3y+5z-11 & =0 \\\\ 4(9-3t)+3(5+2t)+5(-7+t) & =11 \\\\ 36-12t+15+6t-35+5t & =11 \\\\ -t & =-5 \\\\ t & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=5$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=9-3(5)=-6 \\\\ y=5+2(5)=15 \\\\ z=-7+5=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is  $P(-6,15,-2).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387666 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "caf29808-4551-56a0-ac86-a4587a06fc0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line and a Plane Given in Other Forms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e7d6e3a2-bd17-518b-a420-9be2d6ede2d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(9,-3,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387668} {:answer/id #uuid "fd1e7486-194c-5f91-b648-30d5fc905ddc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,-1,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387669} {:answer/id #uuid "3142852d-48b8-5774-8470-a6efcf238212" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387670} {:answer/id #uuid "bf61788e-b726-5e47-a6a7-89955c7d41db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-6,0,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387671} {:answer/id #uuid "0db1fcb0-c0a8-57e5-ac80-2d73a1e639ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(14,-4,7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387672}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0db1fcb0-c0a8-57e5-ac80-2d73a1e639ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(14,-4,7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387672} :answer-field/id #uuid "8269ff46-ca04-5b2b-b137-fa58cf5a3d69" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387667}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0da8771f-0983-5e77-be97-afe167de38df" :question/math-academy-id "q-108371" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨4,-2,3⟩+w⟨5,-1,2⟩,\\,Π:r=⟨10,-5,12⟩+s⟨4,3,0⟩+t⟨0,2,5⟩.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the equation of a plane in the parametric form $r=p+tv+sw$, we have that its normal vector is $n=v\\times w.$ In our case, the normal vector to $Π$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =⟨4,3,0⟩\\times ⟨0,2,5⟩ \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 4 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =15i-20j+8k \\\\  & =⟨15,-20,8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane $Π$ in dot product form is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨15,-20,8⟩ & =⟨10,-5,12⟩\\cdot ⟨15,-20,8⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨15,-20,8⟩ & =346.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨4,-2,3⟩+w⟨5,-1,2⟩$ into the equation of the plane in dot product form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨15,-20,8⟩ & =346 \\\\ ⟨4+5w,-2-w,3+2w⟩\\cdot ⟨15,-20,8⟩ & =346 \\\\ 15(4+5w)-20(-2-w)+8(3+2w) & =346 \\\\ 60+75w+40+20w+24+16w & =346 \\\\ 111w & =222 \\\\ w & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $q$ of the intersection point $Q,$ we substitute $w=2$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q & =⟨4+5(2),-2-(2),3+2(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨14,-4,7⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $Q(14,-4,7).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387673 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "caf29808-4551-56a0-ac86-a4587a06fc0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line and a Plane Given in Other Forms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d6d831ac-92de-5fef-b4b6-09d774020b60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(13,7,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387675} {:answer/id #uuid "f70f6d86-43fd-59f7-a0fb-b400b5d7e414" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(8,3,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387676} {:answer/id #uuid "6fba1001-8369-5c0e-95f6-7fdb50afa8e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-12,-5,-13)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387677} {:answer/id #uuid "67e25cb5-4491-5247-b689-ce094bd09db1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-7,-3,-10)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387678} {:answer/id #uuid "0380037d-3624-5985-af69-76df39ab115c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387679}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6fba1001-8369-5c0e-95f6-7fdb50afa8e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-12,-5,-13)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387677} :answer-field/id #uuid "46fdd381-d1f3-5a54-b9a2-08fb1c4a79c0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387674}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2d225520-d7e9-5a28-afbf-6e16563a3611" :question/math-academy-id "q-108889" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\frac{x-3}{5}=\\frac{y-1}{2}=\\frac{z+4}{3},\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨-3,2,-1⟩=39.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the equation of the line $l$, we know that it passes through the point $A(3,1,-4)$ and it is parallel to the vector $v=⟨5,2,3⟩.$ Therefore, its vector equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =⟨3,1,-4⟩+t⟨5,2,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3+5t,1+2t,-4+3t⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨3+5t,1+2t,-4+3t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-3,2,-1⟩ & =39 \\\\ ⟨3+5t,1+2t,-4+3t⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,2,-1⟩ & =39 \\\\ (-3)(3+5t)+2(1+2t)-(-4+3t) & =39 \\\\ -9-15t+2+4t+4-3t & =39 \\\\ -14t & =42 \\\\ t & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=-3$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨3+5(-3),1+2(-3),-4+3(-3)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-12,-5,-13⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get $P(-12,-5,-13).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120162 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "caf29808-4551-56a0-ac86-a4587a06fc0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line and a Plane Given in Other Forms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "815fabd4-9942-57b4-86bc-0a4e8ea26733" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5, 0, 7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117493} {:answer/id #uuid "828a2813-0e1a-52fa-8e56-5675b46d6c0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,-2, 19)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117494} {:answer/id #uuid "a16033ae-062f-5189-8043-5212bcbcca8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0, 7, 2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117495} {:answer/id #uuid "b4553fc5-f5f7-54cf-b55a-bad20dc70a3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117496} {:answer/id #uuid "2d858785-175b-5493-a285-e2730b6169da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5, 3, 7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117497}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "815fabd4-9942-57b4-86bc-0a4e8ea26733" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5, 0, 7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117493} :answer-field/id #uuid "72b7f63a-ddcb-5c41-8c61-f730276427a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117492}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a9c8b702-f6a3-5488-9345-1b22f3aeec01" :question/math-academy-id "q-33081" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\frac{x-1}{2}=\\frac{y+2}{1}=\\frac{z-1}{3},\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨1,6,2⟩=19.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the equation of the line $l$, we know that it passes through the point $A(1,-2,1)$ and it is parallel to the vector $v=⟨2,1,3⟩.$ Therefore, its vector equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =⟨1,-2,1⟩+t⟨2,1,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1+2t,-2+t,1+3t⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨1+2t,-2+t,1+3t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨1,6,2⟩ & =19 \\\\ ⟨1+2t,-2+t,1+3t⟩\\cdot ⟨1,6,2⟩ & =19 \\\\ (1+2t)+6(-2+t)+2(1+3t) & =19 \\\\ 1+2t-12+6t+2+6t & =19 \\\\ 14t & =28 \\\\ t & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨1+2(2),-2+2,1+3(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,0,7⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get $P(5,0,7).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387680 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "caf29808-4551-56a0-ac86-a4587a06fc0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line and a Plane Given in Other Forms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f0b88eff-8ed7-5763-8342-49fe491b68cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,-3,-11)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387682} {:answer/id #uuid "719be12e-1496-55f2-b6c2-e488693d6fe8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(11,-1,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387683} {:answer/id #uuid "5f32b3e5-ada1-5833-bda5-8c4236ce226b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3,2,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387684} {:answer/id #uuid "60d6d238-7b70-5c55-af31-e93aac243f58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387685} {:answer/id #uuid "59d9b629-b554-58d8-8bb5-35a5aca1c3db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(11,-3,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387686}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "59d9b629-b554-58d8-8bb5-35a5aca1c3db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(11,-3,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387686} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8ac8054-65d2-5274-b462-4accb5725bdc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387681}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f5c58476-2e22-55a5-af93-3aace6df8e02" :question/math-academy-id "q-33197" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\frac{x-2}{-3}=\\frac{y-3}{2}=\\frac{z+4}{-1},\\,Π:3x-2y+z-38=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the equation of the line $l$, we know that it passes through the point $A(2,3,-4)$ and it is parallel to the vector $v=⟨-3,2,-1⟩.$ Therefore, its parametric equations are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =⟨2,3,-4⟩+t⟨-3,2,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2-3t,3+2t,-4-t⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x-2y+z-38 & =0 \\\\ 3x-2y+z & =38 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-2,1⟩ & =38 \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-2,1⟩ & =38\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨2-3t,3+2t,-4-t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨3,-2,1⟩ & =38 \\\\ ⟨2-3t,3+2t,-4-t⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-2,1⟩ & =38 \\\\ 3(2-3t)-2(3+2t)+(-4-t) & =38 \\\\ 6-9t-6-4t-4-t & =38 \\\\ -14t & =42 \\\\ t & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=-3$ into the vector equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨2-3(-3),3+2(-3),-4-(-3)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨11,-3,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get $P(11,-3,-1).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120223 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e761b5-ec1c-549d-b726-e0909cfe460b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Parametric Form and a Plane in Cartesian Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8977164a-8ad7-56e9-94a7-d1231f0c5ade" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-9, 9, 7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117839} {:answer/id #uuid "fd122388-c8df-5ba9-8c16-8ce6fa095bc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,-1, 3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117840} {:answer/id #uuid "46f916f3-3853-57e9-ba4e-59cb01cf50fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(9,-9, 7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117841} {:answer/id #uuid "670f3c35-0bae-5d98-a7f7-406e9c05c9eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(9, 7,-9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117842} {:answer/id #uuid "6812f233-b49b-50e7-80f8-912186dc94d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117843}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46f916f3-3853-57e9-ba4e-59cb01cf50fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(9,-9, 7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117841} :answer-field/id #uuid "8efee06f-3bfd-5143-ad04-c2e4495511e7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117838}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c755ffbb-8374-5c52-a967-a6387ef6da9c" :question/math-academy-id "q-33992" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:{\\begin{aligned}x=5-2t \\\\ y=-1+4t \\\\ z=-3-5t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:2x-5y+3z-84=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-5y+3z-84 & =0 \\\\ 2(5-2t)-5(-1+4t)+3(-3-5t) & =84 \\\\ 10-4t+5-20t-9-15t & =84 \\\\ -39t & =78 \\\\ t & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=-2$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=5-2(-2)=9 \\\\ y=-1+4(-2)=-9 \\\\ z=-3-5(-2)=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is  $P(9,-9,7).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387687 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abef3da6-252e-51e4-b816-9ef7233b9a5d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Vector Form and a Plane in Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dcb7e221-c012-556f-afd1-6033b066878a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3,0,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387689} {:answer/id #uuid "ddc7a5c7-170d-5831-afe7-a219e769882e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-10,-13,7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387690} {:answer/id #uuid "3a165ba9-749a-5e7d-8355-e1dc9444b19e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-17,-10,13)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387691} {:answer/id #uuid "43bdd26a-75ac-5fd8-9239-c7214b6e7cc0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-13,-10,17)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387692} {:answer/id #uuid "c3136bbc-b164-562c-8db7-072502c1a632" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387693}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43bdd26a-75ac-5fd8-9239-c7214b6e7cc0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-13,-10,17)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387692} :answer-field/id #uuid "2953b1bd-39cb-5bcf-8e0b-de035ff42ece" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387688}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "325cb2ca-450c-5da2-91d9-b7629e65e0f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-73985" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨2,0,2⟩+t⟨3,2,-3⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨5,-2,3⟩=6.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨2+3t,2t,2-3t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨2+3t,2t,2-3t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨5,-2,3⟩ & =6 \\\\ ⟨2+3t,2t,2-3t⟩\\cdot ⟨5,-2,3⟩ & =6 \\\\ 5(2+3t)-2(2t)+3(2-3t) & =6 \\\\ 10+15t-4t+6-9t & =6 \\\\ 2t & =-10 \\\\ t & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=-5$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨2+3(-5),2(-5),2-3(-5)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-13,-10,17⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(-13,-10,17).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387694 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e761b5-ec1c-549d-b726-e0909cfe460b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Parametric Form and a Plane in Cartesian Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7315de20-0bee-54fa-a72e-d1aa9d3084e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(10,12,11)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387696} {:answer/id #uuid "00e01c5b-2f3c-55e8-bdde-89c15e05ec2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,0,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387697} {:answer/id #uuid "5c5047ab-818b-52c9-b2eb-3ea7c3c64f63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387698} {:answer/id #uuid "01005393-fe01-5dbd-b6d9-06e68c1a5e4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,3,11)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387699} {:answer/id #uuid "63885195-7515-59db-91dd-619141f62808" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,15,11)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387700}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63885195-7515-59db-91dd-619141f62808" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,15,11)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387700} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8c4ab64-c79a-5f27-acbd-ad32ba576566" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387695}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e45ecd53-082b-51d5-8bee-c71442a1f3b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-73999" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:{\\begin{aligned}x=-2-t \\\\ y=9-3t \\\\ z=-1-6t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:-3x+2y+5z-85=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3x+2y+5z-85 & =0 \\\\ -3(-2-t)+2(9-3t)+5(-1-6t) & =85 \\\\ 6+3t+18-6t-5-30t & =85 \\\\ -33t & =66 \\\\ t & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=-2$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-2-(-2)=0 \\\\ y=9-3(-2)=15 \\\\ z=-1-6(-2)=11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is  $P(0,15,11).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338814 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e761b5-ec1c-549d-b726-e0909cfe460b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Parametric Form and a Plane in Cartesian Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df5ac142-a41e-558b-94e2-54be6e32075e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,1,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338816} {:answer/id #uuid "5cdda2c9-4fe5-5bb2-9519-342c31cd32ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,2,-8)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338817} {:answer/id #uuid "5f9408c3-0eb4-5b30-8808-98420723e10f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,12,-18)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338818} {:answer/id #uuid "105d22a0-f100-57a5-83c4-a6a5d8b76d64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338819} {:answer/id #uuid "410b9713-26d7-5617-92d8-b56182622870" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(10,21,-14)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338820}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f9408c3-0eb4-5b30-8808-98420723e10f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,12,-18)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338818} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7732099-3c9a-500e-a0a3-ab40ac1da9d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338815}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "45a75007-267d-50a7-b554-5511306a0ee0" :question/math-academy-id "q-74003" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:{\\begin{aligned}x=5-t \\\\ y=4+2t \\\\ z=-6-3t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:4x+6y-3z-130=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+6y-3z-130 & =0 \\\\ 4(5-t)+6(4+2t)-3(-6-3t) & =130 \\\\ 20-4t+24+12t+18+9t & =130 \\\\ 17t & =68 \\\\ t & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=4$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=5-4=1 \\\\ y=4+2(4)=12 \\\\ z=-6-3(4)=-18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is  $P(1,12,-18).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387701 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "caf29808-4551-56a0-ac86-a4587a06fc0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line and a Plane Given in Other Forms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c53a16cf-6fa4-5de2-b768-e0df5e044119" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,0,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387703} {:answer/id #uuid "be603d2d-d637-580d-bad6-828af604fb14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5,4,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387704} {:answer/id #uuid "f0252694-088c-5d76-9207-7a3057bc15fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387705} {:answer/id #uuid "eeef8553-eafe-5796-8b2e-c7f2c5618cba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,-5,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387706} {:answer/id #uuid "87af3ebf-4dfb-5939-8c71-f5895ce797d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,1,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387707}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87af3ebf-4dfb-5939-8c71-f5895ce797d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,1,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387707} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a6172fa-157e-5561-a07f-61ca4db2b67d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387702}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "845a9150-4e19-5e0f-8a87-b8822d534204" :question/math-academy-id "q-74004" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨3,1,5⟩+w⟨-2,-5,4⟩,\\,Π:r=⟨-5,4,2⟩+s⟨0,3,1⟩+t⟨2,0,1⟩.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the equation of a plane in the parametric form $r=p+tv+sw$, we have that its normal vector is $n=v\\times w.$ In our case, the normal vectors to $Π$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =⟨0,3,1⟩\\times ⟨2,0,1⟩ \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =3i+2j-6k \\\\  & =⟨3,2,-6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane $Π$ in dot product form is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,2,-6⟩ & =⟨-5,4,2⟩\\cdot ⟨3,2,-6⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,2,-6⟩ & =-19.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨3,1,5⟩+w⟨-2,-5,4⟩$ into the equation of the plane in dot product form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨3,2,-6⟩ & =-19 \\\\ ⟨3-2w,1-5w,5+4w⟩\\cdot ⟨3,2,-6⟩ & =-19 \\\\ 3(3-2w)+2(1-5w)-6(5+4w) & =-19 \\\\ 9-6w+2-10w-30-24w & =-19 \\\\ -40w & =0 \\\\ w & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $q$ of the intersection point $Q,$ we substitute $w=0$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q & =⟨3-2(0),1-5(0),5+4(0)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,1,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $Q(3,1,5).$"}]}
